  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Prove that there are no integers $a$ and $b$ for which $2a+4b=3$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$2(a+2b)=3$ would equate an even integer with an odd integer, a contradiction.",
      "worked": "Suppose such integers $a$ and $b$ exist. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}2a+4b&=3\\\\2(a+2b)&=3.\\end{align*}$$\nThe left-hand side is even because $a+2b$ is an integer, whereas the right-hand side is odd. This is a contradiction. Therefore, no such integers exist.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
